From a8807612fe0631de6846676ef63ba6efd0ee46e6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: havok2-htwo <havok2-htwo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 02:58:41 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 29/37] prefill: STRATA_MMQ_GROUP_SORT=1 sorts the full MMQ
 groups by row count, keeping the partial group

STRATA_MMQ_RESIDENT_SORT_NE=1 puts a fully resident layer's experts in row-count order, so each
16-expert group's max_rows (its tile padding) is close to its experts' own. It also moves the hottest
experts into the last, partial group, whose few tiles take MMQ's stream-k split: the K boundaries move
with the group's tile count and the prompt's bits change.

The new switch sorts only order[0, n - n % 16] (mmq_resident_sort_span) and leaves the partial group's
experts, and so its rows, where they were. A full group's launch has 160 (gate/up) or 320 (down) tiles
per column tile; mmq::whole_tiles checks on every visible GPU that every such launch runs one block per
tile (tile efficiency >= 90 %, NVIDIA) and that all tile widths share the I/K tiles and SRAM layout. Then
each expert's rows get the same bits in any full group whatever its group-mates and max_rows. Where it does
not hold (e.g. 108 or 128 SMs, AMD's stream-k grid) the switch does nothing. RESIDENT_SORT_NE takes
precedence when both are set; with neither the code path is unchanged.

prefill_mmq_tab_test part 4 runs a layer's groups as prefill.cpp does (src-gathered q8_1 rows, absolute
bounds, the group's max_rows) in ID order and in both sorted orders, for IQ3_S / IQ4_XS gate/up and
IQ4_NL / Q8_0 down: with the partial group kept every token's rows are bitwise equal (16 cases); sorting
the partial group too changes 133-1881 rows per case. 890 comparisons, 0 failed (RTX 3090).

Measured on 4x RTX 3090, UD-IQ4_XS, T16-142fcb (split 12,24,37, every expert resident), read time,
medians of 6, back to back: 150-token prompt 145.8 -> 136.2 ms, 1,200-token prompt 428.6 -> 363.4 ms
(RESIDENT_SORT_NE: 134.9 / 358.6 ms). The final residuals of five prompts (300-1,200 tokens,
STRATA_PREFILL_DUMP_R_ALL every position and STRATA_PREFILL_DUMP_R fp32) are byte-identical to the
reference build; with RESIDENT_SORT_NE every row differs. batch_test16 (16 slots, a 1,200-token prompt)
is token-identical to the reference dump.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
